 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 1.3,
   "text": "Jesus got angry."
  },
  {
   "start": 2.18,
   "end": 3.86,
   "text": "So, is anger a sin?"
  },
  {
   "start": 4.76,
   "end": 7.74,
   "text": "In a synagogue, a man stood there with a withered hand,"
  },
  {
   "start": 8.3,
   "end": 9.88,
   "text": "and some people watched Jesus"
  },
  {
   "start": 9.88,
   "end": 11.84,
   "text": "hoping to catch him breaking the rules."
  },
  {
   "start": 12.52,
   "end": 15.84,
   "text": "The Bible says Jesus looked roundabout on them with anger,"
  },
  {
   "start": 16.38,
   "end": 17.82,
   "text": "but read the rest of that verse,"
  },
  {
   "start": 18.58,
   "end": 20.66,
   "text": "being grieved for the hardness of their hearts."
  },
  {
   "start": 21.42,
   "end": 24.72,
   "text": "He was angry and heartbroken at the same time."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.26,
   "end": 26.48,
   "text": "Then he healed the man anyway."
  },
  {
   "start": 27.2,
   "end": 29.12,
   "text": "Another time, he made a whip of cords"
  },
  {
   "start": 29.12,
   "end": 30.82,
   "text": "and flipped the tables in the temple."
  },
  {
   "start": 31.58,
   "end": 34.14,
   "text": "Make not my father's house and house of merchandise."
  },
  {
   "start": 34.78,
   "end": 36.64,
   "text": "But notice who he got angry for,"
  },
  {
   "start": 37.42,
   "end": 40.8,
   "text": "God's house and hurting people, never for himself."
  },
  {
   "start": 41.7,
   "end": 43.2,
   "text": "When they mocked him and hurt him,"
  },
  {
   "start": 43.48,
   "end": 45.94,
   "text": "when he was reviled, reviled not again."
  },
  {
   "start": 46.66,
   "end": 47.58,
   "text": "Instead, he said,"
  },
  {
   "start": 48.24,
   "end": 51.38,
   "text": "Father, forgive them, for they know not what they do."
  },
  {
   "start": 52.08,
   "end": 53.5,
   "text": "Angry about what hurt others,"
  },
  {
   "start": 54.12,
   "end": 55.84,
   "text": "forgiving about what hurt him."
  },
  {
   "start": 56.3,
   "end": 58.2,
   "text": "And the Bible gives anger a deadline."
  },
  {
   "start": 58.8,
   "end": 60.74,
   "text": "Be angry and sin not."
  },
  {
   "start": 61.28,
   "end": 63.36,
   "text": "Let not the sun go down upon your wrath."
  },
  {
   "start": 64.16,
   "end": 64.66,
   "text": "Did you notice?"
  },
  {
   "start": 65.38,
   "end": 67.18,
   "text": "The sun has been setting this whole time."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.9,
   "end": 70.22,
   "text": "Is there someone you need to forgive before it goes down?"
  },
  {
   "start": 70.96,
   "end": 71.66,
   "text": "Just type today."
  }
 ],
